## Context

Reading-2 finding 21 (tracker 0578). §7 (sec:extensions, main.tex
L857) is the only section with NUMBERED subsection headings; all other
sections respect the writing guide (no numbered subsections). Convert
its four subsections to the starred house form. Sequenced after 0585
and 0586 because those rewrite §7.1/§7.2 prose — convert the surviving
headings once.

Subsections (post-0586 state may differ — re-grep):
- sec:ext-difficulty (L865) "Why is the task hard?"
- sec:ext-screen (L882) "Screening without a reference"
- sec:fusion (L913) "Can runs be fused?"
- sec:ext-system (L941) "What system do the findings imply?"

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.tex` — the four `\subsection` headings;
  every `\ref{sec:ext-*}` / `\ref{sec:fusion}` call site (grep before
  editing)
- `tests/test_manuscript_source_section.py:80` — extracts
  `section("sec:fusion")` as subsection text; must keep working
- `tests/test_manuscript_cohort_and_caveats.py` — primacy-marker test
  (~L252) keyed on sec:fusion; STANAG test (L257, L285) keyed on
  sec:ext-screen — both key on labels, so labels MUST stay attached
- `docs/editorial-brief.md` — `label-stability-contract`

## Actions

1. Convert each `\subsection{…}\label{…}` to
   `\subsection*{…}\label{…}` + `\addcontentsline{toc}{subsection}{…}`
   (house pattern, cf. the Prompts subsection L1373) — labels stay,
   PDF bookmarks stay.
2. A `\label` on a starred subsection resolves `\ref` to the enclosing
   section counter — every `\ref{sec:fusion}` / `\ref{sec:ext-*}` call
   site must be reworded so the rendered text stays truthful (e.g.
   "the fusion discussion in §\ref{sec:extensions}" or a named
   pointer). Re-check the crossref adherence test semantics: every ref
   must still resolve to a defined label.
3. Check hyperref anchor uniqueness builds clean (no duplicate
   destination warnings introduced).

## Test

- Red first: a structural guard asserting no numbered `\subsection{`
  exists between sec:extensions and the next `\section` — red now,
  green after.

